BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:165551@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20261010T120752Z
DTSTART:20261002T193000Z
SUMMARY:January 2027 - December 2027 Financial Transmission Rights (FTR) Auction to Open
DESCRIPTION:The January 2027 - December 2027 Round 1 (LT1 2027) FTR Auction bidding period opens at 00:00 on October 20\, 2026 and closes at 11:00 on October 22\, 2026. The results for Round 1 (LT1 2027) will be available to registered FTR market participants via eFTR by November 6\, 2026.\n\n\n\nThe January 2027 - December 2027 Round 2 (LT2 2027) FTR Auction bidding period opens at 00:00 on November 23\, 2026 and closes at 11:00 on November 25\, 2026. The results for Round 2 (LT2 2027) will be available to registered FTR market participants via eFTR by December 4\, 2026.\n\n\n\nRegistered FTR customers will find assumptions and related information for these auctions posted on the FTR Assumptions page available by link from eFTR. For additional information\, please see the eFTR User Guide and the ISO New England Manual for Financial Transmission Rights\, M-06.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165551
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165551
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:165564@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20261010T120752Z
DTSTART:20261002T195200Z
SUMMARY:January 2027 - December 2027 Financial Transmission Rights (FTR) Auction to Open
DESCRIPTION:The January 2027 - December 2027 Round 1 (LT1 2027) FTR Auction bidding period opens at 00:00 on October 20\, 2026 and closes at 11:00 on October 22\, 2026. The results for Round 1 (LT1 2027) will be available to registered FTR market participants via eFTR by November 6\, 2026.\n\n\n\nThe January 2027 - December 2027 Round 2 (LT2 2027) FTR Auction bidding period opens at 00:00 on November 23\, 2026 and closes at 11:00 on November 25\, 2026. The results for Round 2 (LT2 2027) will be available to registered FTR market participants via eFTR by December 4\, 2026.\n\n\n\nRegistered FTR customers will find assumptions and related information for these auctions posted on the FTR Assumptions page available by link from eFTR. For additional information\, please see the eFTR User Guide and the ISO New England Manual for Financial Transmission Rights\, M-06.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165564
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165564
END:VEVENT
