SUMMARY:2026 Open Meeting of the ISO Board of Directors
LOCATION:Hilton Boston Back Bay\, 40 Dalton Street\, Boston\, MA 02115
DESCRIPTION:The purpose of this meeting is to conduct an open meeting of the ISO Board of Directors to give the public an opportunity to observe the Board’s discussions firsthand.\n\nThe meeting will be held both in-person and virtually. After the meeting\, the ISO will post a video recording for the benefit of members of the public who are not able to attend the meeting live.\n\nAdvanced registration is required to attend in-person\, using the link below. In-person registration will close on October 30.\n\nRegister to Attend In-Person\n\nVirtual attendance is not limited and registration is not required. To attend this meeting virtually\, please join from the WebEx link below.\n\nWebEx link: https://iso-newengland.webex.com/iso-newengland/j.php?MTID=m65bdc3227aace0b87e3309f35e3adfa4\n\nPassword: ISOBoard2026!\n\nMeeting Number: 2439 478 0409\n\nThe meeting will include a Listening Session to provide an opportunity for both in-person and virtual attendees to address the Board directly. Please use the link below to sign up to request to provide comments during the meeting. A limited number of timeslots are available. ISO staff will follow up with those who have requested to speak prior to the meeting.\n\nSign Up to Request to Provide Comments\n\nAnyone can submit written comments to the ISO Board of Directors either in advance or after the meeting. Please submit written comments by email to BoardofDirectors@iso-ne.com.\n\n\n	Written comments provided by Nov. 30 will be compiled and posted to the ISO website.\n\n\nMeeting details can also be found on the event website. We will provide additional event information\, such as parking and transportation options\, closer to the meeting date.\n\nIf you have any questions\, please reach out to Melissa Winne or Eric Johnson.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161548
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=161548
END:VEVENT
